    "title": "Pinder, Cambridge-SD remain undefeated",
    "date": "2024-01-09",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Pinder, Cambridge-SD remain undefeated\n\n January 9, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 189\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n RIDGELY — Semaj Pinder had a game-high 20 points Monday night as Cambridge-South Dorchester High's boys' basketball team remained undefeated with a 90-58 victory over North Caroline.Sterling Perkins finished with 16 points for the Vikings, who improved to 7-0 overall, 6-0 North Bayside.\nNasai Bell had 19 points for North Caroline (3-4, 3-3).\nQueen Anne's 83, N. Dorchester 36CENTREVILLE — Collin Woolford scored 27 points as the Lions won their second straight. Vincent Gilberto added 24 points for Queen Anne's (7-2, 6-1).\nEaston 75, St. Michaels 45EASTON — Sophomore Marshall Bailey had 15 points, leading the Warriors past their county rival.\nJames Warren had 14 points for Easton (6-3, 5-1) and Ayden Buchkoski finished with 12 points.\nNakhi Miller led St. Michaels (2-7, 1-6) with 12 points and Zavion Goldsborough added 10.\nGirls' BasketballCambridge-SD 46, North Caroline 43CAMBRIDGE — LeAsia Todd had 22 points, 17 rebounds and six blocked shots to pace the Vikings.\nDestiny Johnson scored 17 points to go with five rebounds for Cambridge-SD (5-2, 4-2).\nColonel 47, Kent County 30WORTON — Ty Singletary scored 17 points to pace the Colonels.\nSelina Austinville and Jazmir Jackson each added eight points for Colonel Richardson (5-3, 3-3). \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
