  {
    "title": "Vikings regain form, rout Trojans",
    "date": "2024-01-23",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Vikings regain form, rout Trojans\n\n January 23, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 404\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n CAMBRIDGE — One night after its closest game this season, Cambridge-South Dorchester High's boys basketball team recaptured its dominating form.LaShaun Moody had 17 points and Sterling Perkins had 16 Tuesday night, as the North Bayside-leading Vikings rolled to an 88-66 victory over Kent County, raising their record to 12-0 overall, 10-0 division.\nKoby Ennals added 14 for Cambridge-SD.\nJonah Somerville led Kent County (4-7, 2-7) with 23 points.\nMoody scored a season-high 32 points on Monday, as the Vikings edged Salisbury School, 71-69, for their narrowest margin of victory this season. Samej Pinder had 14 points and Anthony Hughes and Perkins each had 12.\nPiera Vazquez scored 25 to lead Salisbury School.\nEASTON 65 COL. RICHARDSON 52EASTON — Marshall Bailey and Ja'Kai Brooks each scored 20 points Tuesday, as the Warriors (9-4, 8-2) won their fifth straight — not counting their forfeit loss to Cambridge-SD on Jan. 11.\nOn Monday, Bailey totaled 25 points in a 62-50 victory over Kent Island. Rayan Haq and Brooks finished with 12 points apiece.\nAlso Monday, Colonel Richardson's Dreden Lake scored 31 points in a 75-73 loss to Queen Anne's. Makiah Batson had 13 and Jazir Dickerson 11.\nThe Lions were led by Vince Gilberto's 28 points and Collin Woolford's 23 points. Queen Anne's (10-2, 9-1) has won four straight.\nST. MICHAELS 58 NORTH DORCHESTER 46SHILOH — Johnny Mautz scored 21 points and Nakhi Miller had 20 Monday night, leading the Saints (3-8, 2-7) to a regular-season sweep of the Eagles.\nGIRLS BASKETBALLQUEEN ANNE'S 53 COL. RICHARDSON 35AMERICAN CORNER — Freshman Bea Holthaus notched her 10th double-double of the season with 12 points and 12 rebounds as the Lions pushed their record to 12-0, 10-0 Monday.\nHolthaus also had five blocked shots. Laila Coles had nine points and four steals, RJ Ensor finished with seven points and 10 assists, and Emily Rendulic added seven points.\nTy Singletary's 17 points led Colonel Richardson (6-6, 4-6).\nNORTH CAROLINE 56 ST. MICHAELS 12RIDGELY — Selaya Garrison's 12 points paced the Bulldogs to their fourth win in six games. Jasiyah Henry added nine points for North Caroline (6-4, 5-3).\nSSPP 51 SALISBURY CHRISTIAN 15SALISBURY — Senior Morgan Quade scored a team-high 20 points and sophomore Avery McCall had 14 Tuesday, pacing Saints Peter and Paul in Eastern Shore Independent Athletic Conference play.\nSam Murphy finished with 11 points for the Sabres, who improved to 10-4 overall, 4-1 ESIAC.\nMcCall had 25 points and 11 boards Monday during a 48-44 loss to Seaford (Del.). Quade added 15 points. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 1,
    "day": 23,
    "llm_classification": {
      "topic": "Sports",
