  {
    "title": "Warriors extend win streak",
    "date": "2024-01-25",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Warriors extend win streak\n\n January 25, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 610\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n EASTON — Easton High boys head basketball coach Dionte Hynson thinks his team is beating the teams it should be defeating right now.More importantly, he thinks the Warriors are playing they way they should as the regular season pushes toward its latter stages.\nSenior Ja'Kai Brooks scored a game-high 16 points and classmate James Warren finished with 13 Thursday night, as Easton rolled to its sixth consecutive victory — excluding its Jan. 11 forfeit to Cambridge-South Dorchester — with a 75-40 victory over North Dorchester on senior night.\n\"We put in some new stuff defensively we're working on,\" Hynson said after the Warriors improved to 10-4 overall, 9-2 North Bayside. \"Got to get a little more sharper. Got a new starting lineup, too. I think we're playing the right way right now.\"\nHynson started an all senior lineup on senior night as Easton carried a 14-11 lead into the second quarter against a North Dorchester team (0-14, 0-11) that dressed only seven players due to injuries. Tahjere Pritchett (team-high 11 points) scored 30 seconds into the second quarter to pull the Eagles within 14-13.\nThe Warriors maintained a one-point lead midway through the second before going on a 7-0 burst that extended their lead to 23-15. Vernon Price splashed a 3-pointer to end nearly a 4-minute scoring drought for North Dorchester before Easton scored the final five points before half for a 28-18 lead at intermission.\nEaston started its new starting lineup to open the second half, and Brooks, Marshall Bailey (10 points), Kyree Acree, Kahlil Batson, and Zymier Ramirez pieced together a dominating 23-8 run in the first six-plus minutes to build a commanding 51-26 lead.\n\"I like our defense,\" said Hynson, who watched his team's fullcourt pressure create a string of Eagle turnovers in the third. \"Quick hands. We've got some speed at the guard position. We just got to tighten some stuff up and get ready for the next game.\"\nBatson and Ramirez each scored four points in the paint in the third quarter as Easton began dominating inside. Bailey then converted a steal into a transition basket before Brooks took two more steals to the rim for a 19-point cushion.\n\"I like where I am,\" Hynson said. \"We're always ready to play whoever wherever. We got (Queen Anne's) on Tuesday so we'll see what happens.\"\nHynson pulled his starting unit with 2 minutes remaining in the third quarter and watched his reserves outscore the Eagles 14-7 in the fourth.\nNorth Dorchester head coach Robert Smith Jr. watched his team battle, but with only two reserves, the Eagles seemed to tire down the stretch. Jae'zeon Cephas finished with nine points and Vernon Price seven.\nEaston hosts defending North Bayside-champion Queen Anne's (11-3, 10-1) on Tuesday, and faces division-leading Cambridge-SD (12-0, 10-0) on its home floor Feb. 15 to close the regular season.\nST. MICHAELS 70 COL. RICHARDSON 62ST. MICHAELS — Johnny Mautz Jr. scored 27 points and Nakhi Miller had 23 as the Saints (4-9, 3-8) upset the Colonels.\nDreden Lake had 26 for Colonel Richardson (7-7, 5-7) and Jazir Dickerson had 18.\nQUEEN ANNE'S 97 KENT COUNTY 57CENTREVILLE — Vince Gilberto had 31 points and Collin Woolford 21 to pace the Lions.\nGIRLS BASKETBALLKENT ISLAND 48 NORTH CAROLINE 38RIDGELY — Sydney Riska logged a double-double with 14 points and 12 rebounds to lead the Buccaneers.\nLilli Dauses finished with 11 points and Makayla Kropfelder added 10 for Kent Island (9-2, 9-1).\nQUEEN ANNE'S 60 KENT COUNTY 16WORTON — Bea Holthaus totaled 12 points, six rebounds and five steals as the Lions remained undefeated.\nKariana Hickson had 10 points, six assists and five steals for Queen Anne's (13-0, 10-0), Laila Coles finished with eight points and five steals, and Meg Taylor scored seven points. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 1,
    "day": 25,
    "llm_classification": {
      "topic": "Sports",
