  {
    "title": "Lions ride 1-2 punch past Easton",
    "date": "2024-01-30",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Lions ride 1-2 punch past Easton\n\n January 30, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 850\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n EASTON — Queen Anne's County High's Bea Holthaus and Laila Coles are one of the top freshmen combinations to hit the North Bayside hardwood in a long, long time.But Lions girls' head basketball coach Mike Kern knows there are going to be nights when his team isn't at its best.\nTuesday was shaping up to be one of those nights, as Easton went on an 8-0 run to open the second half for one-point lead. But that only seemed to wake up the Lions, who proceeded to go on a 17-3 tear to close the third quarter on the way to a 53-42 victory.\n\"We're young,\" said Kern, whose team improved to 14-0 overall, 12-0 North Bayside. \"We're playing in a tough environment. We're going to have these games where we don't play our best. But will still overcome. I'm proud of them for overcoming.\"\nHolthaus, who had a game-high 25 points to go with 13 rebounds and five blocked shots, and Coles (16 points) helped Queen Anne's build a 24-17 halftime lead.\nBut Easton (7-8, 7-5), which lost to the Lions by 32 on Jan. 2 in Centreville, erased that deficit in the opening two minutes of the second half. Addison Chandler (10 points) buried a 3-pointer. Sisi Sama (10 points) scored inside, hit one of two free throws, then drove the lane for a basket and a 25-24 Warriors lead.\n\"I thought Easton came out a little hungrier than we were tonight,\" Kern said. \"And they out-rebounded us, which is a little disappointing. But they were going hard to the ball. I think Easton deserves a lot of credit. They did a great job on the boards. And they were getting second and third opportunities, and that's what kept them in the game. We've got to do better.\"\nThe Lions may not have done better immediately on the glass, but they improved on the scoreboard. After Kern called time with 5:45 remaining in the third, Queen Anne's returned to the floor and took control of the game, outscoring the Warriors 25-5 over the next 7-plus minutes.\nLeading the charge was Holthaus, who accounted for 17 points in the surge, which included burying three baseline jumpers and a 5-for-6 effort from the foul line.\n\"Bea is just a phenomenal athlete,\" Kern said. \"She's sees the court really well. She makes everybody around her better. She's very unselfish. She can go inside. She can go outside. She's an all-around player. We're lucky to have her for four years.\"\nThe same can be said of Coles, who in addition to her 16 points, totaled seven steals, five assists and five rebounds.\n\"Her (Holthaus) and Coles both as freshmen are just going to be amazing kids coming up,\" Easton head coach Lesley Staehli said.\nAnd while Holthaus and Coles proved a formidable one-two punch, the Warriors hurt themselves with a 10-for-25 performance from the free-throw line.\n\"We missed 15 free throws,\" Staehli said. \"Had we made some of them, and then stopped the turnovers; taken care of the ball a little bit better (against Coles). And then shutting Bea down a little bit with hands in her face with her shot.\"\nQueen Anne's 17-3 surge to close the third, and an 8-2 burst to open the fourth gave it a 49-30 cushion with 6:21 remaining. Easton made the score more respectable as Chandler's third 3-pointer of the game started a 12-4 Warriors' game-ending run.\n\"We did well I thought considering we got blown out the last time we played them,\" said Staehli, who got a team-high 11 points from Kate Adelman and 10 from Serenity Velez. \"But we're going to be working on our foul shots.\"\nCAMBRIDGE-SD 58 NORTH DORCHESTER 13CAMBRIDGE — LeAsia Todd had 19 points, 13 rebounds and four blocked shots as the Vikings won their third straight.\nTejanae Ballin scored 11 points and Damiya Henry had 10 for Cambridge-South Dorchester (8-4, 7-4).\nNORTH CAROLINE 65 KENT COUNTY 39RIDGELY — Chloe Escoe had a team-high 16 points and Selaya Garrison finished with 12 to lead the Bulldogs (8-5, 6-4). Ashley Kercheval added 10 points for North Caroline.\nSSPP 55 SALISBURY SCHOOL 19SALISBURY — Morgan Quade scored 27 points and Avery McCall had 16 to pace the Sabres in an Eastern Shore Independent Athletic Conference game.\nST. MICHAELS 46 CRISFIELD 45ST. MICHAELS — Brooke Reilly scored 17 points and Madi White delivered a 14-point effort Monday as the Saints notched their first win of the season.\nBOYS BASKETBALLEASTON 66, QUEEN ANNE'S 60EASTON — Ja'Kai Brooks finished with 21 points and Marshall Bailey had 15, leading the Warriors past the Lions and forging a second-place tie in the North Bayside.\nKyree Acree had 11 points for Easton (11-4, 10-2) which pulled even with the Lions (11-4, 10-2) in the division.\nCAMBRIDGE-SD 68 NORTH DORCHESTER 56SHILOH — Koby Ennals' team-high 16 points led the unbeaten Vikings over their county rival. LaShaun Moody and Thomas Wilson each scored 13 points for Cambridge-SD (13-0, 11-0).\nSSPP 76, KEY 61ANNAPOLIS — Garett Hemingway had 18 points and Robbie Cunningham dropped in 17 to fuel the Sabres in an Maryland Interscholastic Athletic Association C Conference game Monday night.\nBrayden Smith added 15 points for Saints Peter and Paul (7-7, 3-2). \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 1,
    "day": 30,
    "llm_classification": {
      "topic": "Sports",
      "explanation": "The article reports on a high school basketball game, detailing scores, players, and coaches, which aligns directly with the Sports topic."
    },
    "llm_classification_meta": {
      "model": "gpt-oss:120b",
      "llm_failed": false
    },
    "entities_people": "[\"Bea Holthaus\", \"Laila Coles\"]",
    "metadata_sport": "basketball",
    "metadata_story_type": "game recap",
    "metadata_location": "Easton, Maryland",
    "metadata_teams": "[\"Queen Anne's County High\", \"Easton\"]",
    "metadata_schools": "[\"Queen Anne's County High\", \"Easton\"]",
    "entities_quoted_people": "[\"coach Mike Kern\", \"head coach Lesley Staehli\"]",
    "metadata_level_of_play": "high school",
