  {
    "title": "Gunston School crew set to join WMIRA",
    "date": "2024-02-14",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Gunston School crew set to join WMIRA\n\n February 14, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 271\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n CENTREVILLE — The Gunston School will join the Washington Metropolitan Interscholastic Rowing Association (WMIRA), the region's premier rowing conference, this spring.While Gunston has regularly competed against WMIRA teams at national regattas like Head of the Schuylkill in Philadelphia, the school is now eligible to compete in the conference championship regatta on May 5.\n\"Each year our students and coaches continue to elevate the quality and competitiveness of the program,\" Head of School John Lewis said, \"and we're eager to join the ranks of the best public and private school rowing teams in our area. We're grateful that the WMIRA expanded its geographical reach to include us, and we look forward to welcoming these teams to home regattas at Gunston.\"\nThe WMIRA includes independent and parochial school teams like DeMatha, Georgetown Day School, St. Albans, Gonzaga, Holton Arms, and National Cathedral School, as well as Montgomery County public school powerhouses such as Blair, Bethesda-Chevy Chase, Walter Johnson, and Walt Whitman.\n\"I'm proud of our rowers, and appreciative of the WMIRA,\" said Natalie Reading, Gunston's head crew coach and assistant athletic director for waterfront athletics. \"This opportunity not only enhances the competitiveness of Gunston's rowing team but also opens doors to a broader range of experiences and challenges. We aim to continue to build on our 2023 Maryland State championship performance.\"\nIn addition to the WMIRA, Gunston will again host the Maryland State rowing championship on Saturday, April 27, on its 75-acre campus on the Corsica River. Spectators are invited to bring chairs and/or blankets and watch the 1,500-meter sprint style race with 4's and 8's, men and women's varsity, junior varsity and novice event categories. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 2,
    "day": 14,
