  {
    "title": "Schmidt's seven goals pace Easton rout",
    "date": "2024-04-17",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Schmidt's seven goals pace Easton rout\n\n April 17, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 408\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n EASTON — Senior Drew Schmidt scored seven goals and set up another, and classmate Hudson Royer netted two goals and two assists Wednesday, as Easton High's boys lacrosse team ran its win streak to six with a 15-4 victory over Kent County.Tyler Rardin had three assists and Charlie Kaminskas had two as the Warriors improved to 6-1 overall, 2-0 North Bayside. Campbell Taliaferro, Ethan Finlay, Sabin Long and Jackson Wieland each had one goal for Easton. Charlie Beaufait and Jack Kilbourne had six saves each, and Sam Noble and Angel Fernandez combined to win 16 faceoffs.\nCAMBRIDGE-SD 21 WICOMICO 0\nSALISBURY — Luke Reinbold scored five goals and four other Vikings had hat tricks, as Cambridge-South Dorchester rolled to its first win of the season.\nWil Reinbold, Nate McClarren, Randall Johnson and Ryan Widmaier each had three goals for the Vikings (1-3). Tabrion Watts added two goals for C-SD.\nGIRLS LACROSSE\nNORTH CAROLINE 15 PARKSIDE 8\nRIDGELY — Riley Walstrum had five goals and an assist, and Claire Blue and Ashlynn Bisesi each had a hat trick and one assist as the Bulldogs extended their winning streak to five.\nCalleigh Tribbett also had a hat trick for North Caroline (5-1). Maddie Nicholson had one goal, and Gracie Faulkner and Reece Bisesi had one assist apiece.\nSSPP 17 WORCESTER PREP 2\nEASTON — Morgan Quade had three goals and four assists, and freshman Emma Hainey scored four goals, helping the Sabres win their seventh straight.\nSophomore Caroline Ewing finished with a hat trick and two assists for Saints Peter and Paul (7-1, 3-0 Eastern Shore Independent Athletic Conference), and freshman Emery Zimmerman recorded a hat trick. Avery McCall added two goals and two assists, Julia Spero had three assists and a goal, Eden Zimmerman scored once, and Samantha Murphy had one assist.\nBASEBALL\nST. MICHAELS 12 NORTH DORCHESTER 0\nSHILOH — Pearson Greenwood went 2 for 4 with a double and three RBIs, and Bobby Fink was 3 for 3 with a pair of RBIs, two stolen bases and three runs as the Saints remained undefeated.\nWill Sherwood (3-0) earned the win, yielding just one hit and striking out three over four innings. Hunter Gottleib was 2 for 3 with an RBI and two runs, and Ethan Royer finished 2 for 2 with three RBIs and two stolen bases as St. Michaels improved to 10-0.\nSOFTBALL\nNORTH DORCHESTER 11 ST. MICHAELS 1\nSHILOH — Jewels Vroman hurled a complete game one-hitter, striking out eight and walking none as the Eagles raised their record to 10-0. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
