  {
    "title": "Girls wrestling champions receive acclamation",
    "date": "2024-06-07",
    "author": "ANDREA GRABENSTEIN agrabenstein@chespub.com",
    "content": "Girls wrestling champions receive acclamation\n\n June 7, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: ANDREA GRABENSTEIN agrabenstein@chespub.com | Section: Local News \n \n 231\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n Making history as the first girls wrestling team to win the Maryland State Championship during the 2023-2024 season, the Liberty Building packed with supporters as Queen Anne's County High School Lions received official recognition and forever acclamation from county commissioners and state delegates May 28.Delegate Jay Jacobs (R-36) presented a Maryland General State Assembly official citation to recognize the historic achievement along with the county commissioners congratulating the Lions on winning the Maryland Secondary School Sports Athletic Association Girls Wrestling State Championship.\nCoach David Stricker was immensely proud of the continual strong teamwork demonstrated by the Lions and the recognition that validated all their hard work.\nSince its inception, the team has blossomed to over 20 members and the Lions have never stopped giving it their all, Coach Stricker said.\nTeam Captain and graduating senior Julia Reburn was one of three original members when the team got started her freshman year.\n\"I can't put into words what this means. It feels well deserved for the whole team,\" Reburn said.\nThe team have always supported each other and have pushed each other physically and mentally to be the best they could be.\n\"We've certainly paid our dues,\" she said.\nReburn considered joining the wrestling team, \"the best decision I ever made\" and highly encouraged students with an interest in wrestling, especially girls, to check out the sport.\n\"It's a girl's sport just as much as a boys,\" she said. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
