  {
    "title": "TALL TASK",
    "date": "2024-08-27",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "TALL TASK\n\n August 27, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 642\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n WORTON — Harold Somerville's biggest challenge heading into his third year as Kent County High's head football coach may not be figuring out who he's going to plug in at left tackle or outside linebacker.No, Somerville's biggest task may be simply getting his players to believe in themselves.\n\"The talent's there,\" Somerville said after Saturday morning's scrimmage against North East of Cecil County. \"They got to believe it.\"\nSomerville isn't saying the Trojans are going to compete for titles or make a deep playoff run. But in Saturday's scrimmage against North East there were plenty of encouraging signs.\nTerrell Fennell slipped around left end, found an open sideline and blazed about 40 yards for a touchdown. There were a handful of other big-chunk plays, and the defense showed solid pursuit to the ball and gang tackled.\nSomerville can also drop back to late last season in terms of his team's growth. One week after getting routed by Snow Hill 47-6 in their regular-season finale, the Trojans upended the Eagles, 34-18, in the first round of the Class 1A East Region playoffs.\n\"We're not looking bad,\" Somerville said. \"I was pleased with Saturday. We know we've got some work to do, but I was pleased with it.\"\nThe offensive line lost two starters from last year's 2-9 squad, and that's where the most work may be needed in terms of getting stronger.\nSophomore Taeshaun Demby (6-foot-1, 250 pounds) starts at center, and is flanked by senior right guard Harrison Gibby (6-0, 190) and sophomore left guard Andrew Fennell (5-9, 200). Senior Wyatt Toulson (5-10, 180) starts at left tackle, while senior Wesley Townsend (6-4, 315) is at right tackle.\n\"I think we can compete with the other 1A schools,\" Somerville said of Bayside rivals Cambridge-South Dorchester, Colonel Richardson, Snow Hill and Washington. \"I honestly feel as though if our line just gives the quarterback enough time to get the ball off I think that we can really compete. And I feel real comfortable with our receivers and our running backs.\"\nHe should considering most every one of them returns from last year.\nSophomore Dwan Harris (6-1, 170) is back at quarterback and looks to have a solid cast of backs that include senior Terrell Fennell (5-7, 150), juniors Scottie Ford (5-9, 140) and Tyrel Dean (5-8, 165), and sophomore Kalief Roberts (5-9, 150).\nThe receiving corps also looks strong, led by senior Jonah Somerville (5-7, 152) — the coach's son — who can line up in the slot or wide, as well as at quarterback or in the backfield. Harris' other two wide targets are sophomore Dylan Hurtt (5-8, 130) and Ramon Peterson (5-9, 150), while seniors Jysir Valentine (6-4, 240) and Shakur Wilson (6-1, 180) are at tight end.\nDefensively, Kent will go with either a 4-3 or 5-3 scheme, with Andrew Fennell and Townsend at the tackles, and Toulson at nose, depending on the lineup. Valentine and Wilson will be the ends.\nCoach Somerville admitted his linebacking unit struggled some against North East, but part of that was because Ford and Dean did not play. When it has a full complement of players, Kent will have junior Zayvion Brown (5-9, 160) and Ford as outside backers and Dean inside.\nThe secondary appears to be a strongpoint, with Terrell Fennell and Peterson at the corners, and Somerville and Roberts playing safety.\n\"I think our defense, at least in the second half, we were playing better than the offense,\" said Coach Somerville, who played nose tackle on Kent County's 1989 and '90 Class 1A state championship teams. \"Especially our DBs. Our DBs are very experienced. They know how to read the ball.\"\nJonah Somerville will handled kickoffs and Harris will punt.\n\"I honestly believe, if they really believe in themselves and the jell together, that we can go to that next level and not just win two games like we have been the last couple years,\" Coach Somerville said. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 8,
