  {
    "title": "Ensminger, Monroy each score twice as Warriors romp in opener for new head coach",
    "date": "2024-09-10",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Ensminger, Monroy each score twice as Warriors romp in opener for new head coach\n\n September 10, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 600\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n EASTON — He knows there will be tougher games and stiffer competition.But, man, did this first one feel good.\nKyle Ensminger scored a pair of goals in the opening 14 minutes, and Ale Monroy scored in each half Tuesday, as Easton High's boys soccer team rolled to an 8-0 victory over Wicomico in the head coaching debut of Avery Brice.\n\"Feels great,\" said Brice, who played on the Warriors' 2014 team that reached the Class 2A state championship game. \"I told the guys in the group, everything I asked of them they delivered. I think that means a lot for me. It means they're balled in. They got the same mindset as me. That means everything. First game, 8-0. But it doesn't stop today. And we don't be complacent.\"\nEnsminger collected a pass from Kai Ferraris, slipped past a defender, and deposited Easton's first goal of the season into the net just 4:14 into the game.\nWicomico keeper Matthew Bier stopped a point-blank bid by Ensminger a little over two minutes later. But in the 14th minute, Ensminger gathered a lead pass from Dominic Stanco, calmly pushed downfield with a pair of defenders closing on his right hip, drew Bier off his line, and neatly tucked a left-footed shot into the right side of the net for a 2-0 lead.\nThe Warriors continued to extend their advantage.\nMario Medina fed Monroy, who unloaded a low, hard drive off Bier's hands for a 3-0 cushion with 25:30 left in the first half. CJ Chaconas settled a ball from Ensminger and hammered a shot off the keeper's hands to make it 4-0. Landon Chaney capped the first-half scoring with a drive from near the left post for a 5-0 Warrior lead.\n\"We continue to go,\" said Brice of his team's not getting complacent despite its comfortable halftime lead. \"And I know when we get really tested, opportunities won't come like they did today. I told the guys that. So we do got to work on finishing, things of that nature, taking our chances and making them count when they are presented upon us.\"\nEaston junior keeper Sam Hutchison was never seriously challenged, as the Warriors' backline and midfield controlled play.\n\"Love our defense. Love our possession game,\" Brice said. \"The guys know that we got to play a little bit simpler. And I told the guys from the get (go), like we do the simple things correct, we'll be the best team.\"\nMedina broke in from left wing in the 8th minute of the second half and was taken down, setting up his penalty-kick goal that pushed the lead to 6-0. Monroy netted his second goal with an innocent-looking chip less than two minutes later. Elmer Pineda completed with scoring with 24:08 remaining when he put one past Indians backup keeper Sam Fleuriot, making it 8-0.\nA new rule instituted this season stops play in the 60th minute if a team has an eight-goal lead.\n\"It was the first thing I was thinking when I woke up this morning,\" Brice said of his first game as head coach. \"So proud of these guys. Talented team. I just want them to continue to know that. One game at a time. We move on. OK, it's not a celebration. We did what we were supposed to and we move on.\"\nQUEEN ANNE'S 2, PARKSIDE 2\nCENTREVILLE — Ryan Lee and James Rath each scored once, and Gage Jordan notched an assist as the Lions battled the Rams to a draw in double overtime.\nJ.M. BENNETT 10, N. CAROLINE 2\nRIDGELY — Heath Frantum and Ayden Russell had one goal apiece for the Bulldogs against the defending Bayside Conference-champion Clippers. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 9,
    "day": 10,
    "llm_classification": {
      "topic": "Sports",
