  {
    "title": "Peak Tip-Off set for 2 days",
    "date": "2024-10-09",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Peak Tip-Off set for 2 days\n\n October 9, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: News \n \n 183\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n WYE MILLS — This year's annual Bayside Basketball Peak Tip-Off at Chesapeake College is scheduled to be held over two days.Play begins on Friday, Dec. 6, in the school's main gym, with a boys junior varsity game between Wicomico and North Caroline at 4 p.m., followed by two varsity contests: Wicomico-North Caroline at 5:30 p.m., and Parkside-Queen Anne's County at 7 p.m. The Parkside-Queen Anne's junior varsity game is slated for 5:30 p.m. in the auxiliary gym.\nPlay continues Saturday, Dec. 7, in the main gym, with Mardela and St. Michaels girls facing off at 11 a.m. Five boys games are set to follow: Mardela-St. Michaels (12:30 p.m.); Washington-North Dorchester (2 p.m.); Pocomoke-Colonel Richardson (4 p.m.); Stephen Decatur-Easton (5:30 p.m.) and Snow Hill-Kent County at 7 p.m.\nFour jayvee games are slated for the auxiliary gym on Saturday: Washington-North Dorchester (12:30 p.m.); Pocomoke-Colonel Richardson (2 p.m.); Stephen Decatur-Easton (4 p.m.); and Snow Hill-Kent County (5:30 p.m.).\nFriday's entry fee will be $5 for students and adults. Saturday's entry fee will be $5 for students, $10 for adults. For more information, contact Michelle Hall at mhall@chesapeake.edu. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 10,
    "day": 9,
