  {
    "title": "Orrell's overtime goal lifts Warriors over Kent Island in thriller",
    "date": "2024-10-15",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Orrell's overtime goal lifts Warriors over Kent Island in thriller\n\n October 15, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 730\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n STEVENSVILLE — Addie Knox paused.Easton High's sophomore midfielder stood on the end line 4 minutes deep into overtime preparing to deliver an entry pass on a penalty corner, when she asked her teammates aligned inside the circle's fringe, \"What are we doing?\"\nLess than a moment later, Knox had her answer: scoring.\nOlivia Orrell scored from just inside the circle Monday night, lifting Easton High's field hockey team to a 1-0 victory over Kent Island at Andy Schipul Stadium — the Warriors' second overtime win in four days.\nAfter Tuesday's games, Queen Anne's (9-1 overall, 4-0 North Bayside) sits atop the division alone in first with Easton (7-3, 3-1) in second and Kent Island (8-3, 3-1) in third. Kent Island could forge a three-way tie atop the North when it hosts Queen Anne's Saturday. But the Lions would likely win the tiebreaker based on a better overall winning percentage.\nFour days after defeating Pocomoke in overtime, Easton and the Bucs needed extra time to settle things, courtesy of some outstanding defense and fine goalie play. Warrior goalie Taylor Bowen (seven saves) faced her heaviest pressure in the first half but let nothing get by her. Easton dominated play in the second half, but couldn't beat Bucs goalie Brynja Petursson (11 saves), who stopped shots sitting and laying down, sending the scoreless stalemate into overtime.\n\"She's a great goalie,\" Kent Island head coach Laura Harding said of Petursson. \"I thought the defense played well. Emma Fleshman stepped up; she was the one playing over Sydney Riska (who was out of town) and did a good job.\n\"We had many opportunities to put it in in the first half,\" Harding continued. \"That's when we had the momentum and couldn't finish. You've got to finish to win.\"\nEaston controlled the second half, and was inches from taking the lead on a corner with 7 minutes left in the third period. But Petursson, with the Warriors poking and trying to jam the ball past her, first made stops while seated, then stretched her body across the goalmouth to keep the game scoreless.\n\"First quarter when they came out I told them we're playing as individuals,\" Easton head coach Kim Neff said of her team. \"And then they started communicating better and playing as a unit. That's when we kind of took over and dominated. But I have to give it to their defense and their goalie because they played a heckuva game. They are hard to get through.\"\nEaston also got some big defensive plays. Stella Kabler poke checked the ball away from Kent Island's Rita Yost on a breakaway, and Myka Motovidlak twice spoiled threats.\nKent Island earned two late corners in the final 2 minutes of regulation, but fired wide of the cage, then watched Easton clear the second attempt, sending the game into the 7-on-7 overtime.\n\"I think we were really determined to get the corner, or at least get the shot off,\" Orrell said. \"We just kept pounding the goal and I got the corner.\"\nKnox set up on the end line to the left of Petursson and directed a pass to Orrell, who took possession, stepped out of the circle, then back in, and smacked a low, hard shot that slid past the right leg of the Bucs' goalie for the game-winner.\n\"I'm like, 'I can do this,'\" Orrell said of the corner. \"I knew it was a good shot. It was a hard hit. And then it went in and made the best sound ever. And then when the ref called it I looked at Addie and the whole team and I was so excited.\"\nWithin seconds, Orrell swarmed on by her jubilant teammates.\n\"It was a great game,\" Harding said. \"Great reffed game. Great played game. Easton ended up wanting it a little more than us in the end. It was clear.\"\nKENT ISLAND 3 KENT COUNTY 1\nWORTON — Rita Yost, Caroline Levin and Audrey Fleshman each scored one goal Tuesday, as the Bucs topped the Trojans.\nEllie Burnside had an assist for Kent Island and Brynja Petursson had three saves.\nQUEEN ANNE'S 7 ST. MICHAELS 0\nCENTREVILLE — Ella Rebstock and Jamie Baldwin netted two goals apiece as the Lions won their ninth straight.\nJordan Bilbo and Haley Cole each had a goal and an assist for Queen Anne's. Aly Edwards added a goal and Ellee McLean an assist. The Lions didn't allow a shot on goal in posting their sixth shutout of the season. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 10,
    "day": 15,
