  {
    "title": "Smith, Corcoran, QA's sweep titles",
    "date": "2024-10-15",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Smith, Corcoran, QA's sweep titles\n\n October 15, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: News \n \n 100\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n GRASONVILLE — Senior Nate Smith rallied over the back nine Tuesday for a 3-over par 75 to win his third consecutive boys individual title at the District 8 golf championships at Prospect Bay Country Club.Smith's win helped the Lions win the team championship as well.\nKeira Corcoran gave Queen Anne's a clean sweep of the titles, when she defeated North Caroline's Taryn Brandt on the second playoff hole to win the girls individual crown.\nKent County freshman Quinten Joiner earned runner-up honors in the boys competition, finishing two strokes back.\nA full report will appear in Thursday's edition of The Star Democrat. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
