  {
    "title": "Bieber, Saints end Easton's title hopes",
    "date": "2024-10-18",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Bieber, Saints end Easton's title hopes\n\n October 18, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 171\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n ST. MICHAELS — Freshman Gavin Bieber scored on a left-footed chip from just inside the box with under 4 minutes remaining Friday night, lifting St. Michaels High's boys soccer team to a 3-2 victory over Easton, ending the Warriors' North Bayside title hopes.Easton (7-5 overall, 6-2 North Bayside) needed a win to clinch its first division title since 2015. Instead, the Saints, with their first victory over the Warriors since 2017, helped Queen Anne's County (8-2-2 overall) win its second straight North Bayside title with a 7-1 division record.\nEaston took a 1-0 lead on Ale Monroy's penalty kick in the 7th minute. St. Michaels (6-6, 5-3) tied the game with 8 minutes left in the first half on Bieber's PK. The Warriors regained the lead on CJ Chaconas' breakaway goal 4 minutes before the break.\nWith 16 minutes left, Saints freshman Wyatt Genrich gained possession off an Ethan Royer corner kick and fed Bieber for the tying goal. Almost 12 minutes later, Bieber netted his game-winner to complete his hat trick. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 10,
    "day": 18,
