  },
  {
    "title": "Lions serve up 3rd straight title",
    "date": "2024-10-29",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Lions serve up 3rd straight title\n\n October 29, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 630\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n SALISBURY — Queen Anne's County High's volleyball team spent time during the first week of practice in August getting to know new head coach Jamie Leventry.But it was on the first day of practice that Leventry defined the importance of serving.\n\"We talked about it starting Day 1,\" Leventry said. \"'We're going to serve tough. It's what we're going to do.'\"\nThe Lions proved extremely tough from the serving line Monday night, as Emerson Stewart reeled off the team's longest service run of the season during a dominating 25-10, 25-9, 25-5 victory over Parkside that gave Queen Anne's its third consecutive Bayside Conference championship.\n\"There's a reason why their record is what it is,\" Parkside head coach Roy Geiser said after the Lions improved to 15-0. \"Great serving team. Great passing team. And frankly we didn't play our best game. But they put a lot of pressure on us and we weren't prepared.\"\nThe Rams (14-4) got an idea of things to come in Game 1, when Sydney Pinder (eight kills) served four straight points, turning a 5-4 Lions lead into a 9-4 edge.\n\"I feel it gives us such an advantage and I think it helps build up our team's momentum,\" Pinder said of her team's service game. \"It just keeps us up as a team.\"\nQueen Anne's maintained that five-point edge before Kaisa Hickson started a five-point serving spree with one of the Lions' 22 aces, extending the lead to 19-9.\nParkside put down a winner to stop that run before Bianca Baker (team-high 13 kills) closed the first game with a six-point roll from the line to cap Game 1.\n\"It's just a matter of putting a lot of pressure on the other team, and kind of getting them out of system,\" Leventry said. \"Whenever we're back there putting good, tough serves on them and they're struggling to pass those, then that puts us in a really good spot.\"\nJensen Nutley put the Lions in a really good spot, when she strung together eight service points for an 8-0 Queen Anne's lead to start Game 2.\n\"I think that was really important because when you're up by so much, I feel like you don't think about making mistakes so much,\" Nutley said. \"When you're in a neck-to-neck game, like when we play a team like Kent Island, where it's serve and serve back and forth, that takes a lot of effort from us not to make mistakes and think about it a lot. When we're up by that much I feel like it lets us loose and play our game.\"\nA Baker kill and three consecutive service points from Stewart pushed the Lions' lead to 11 at 12-1. Queen Anne's lead remained around 11 points until 20-9, when Stewart again stepped to the line and wedged two more aces into a game-sealing, five-point run.\n\"Climbing back on a team like that you just can't do,\" Geiser said. \"We got to play at our very best and that's not what we did tonight.\"\nParkside's Brylie Geiser served to open Game 3, but Baker unloaded another kill for a 1-0 Lions lead. Stewart moved back to the service line and wouldn't leave until Queen Anne's lead was at 19-0.\n\"My main goal is to keep it in; keep a nice, clean flow at serve,\" said Stewart, whose previous best service run was 13. \"I think it's definitely intimidating when there's a long serving streak, especially with a big game on the line.\"\nQueen Anne's completed its 12th sweep of the season with a kill from Nutley and a Marylee Kline serve that was not returned.\n\"Feels great,\" Leventry said. \"It's been a fun season so far. And like I said, we're not done yet. A state championship is our goal.\"\nIt was the first time Queen Anne's has won three straight conference titles in volleyball. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 10,
    "day": 29,
    "llm_classification": {
      "topic": "Sports",
