  {
    "title": "Warriors beat clock, Seahawks",
    "date": "2024-10-30",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Warriors beat clock, Seahawks\n\n October 30, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 675\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n It's won on a penalty stroke in overtime.It's also won on penalty corners — once in overtime, once in double OT.\nTuesday evening, Easton High's field hockey team found yet another way to win — and fray their coaches nerves — scoring just before the clock ran dry.\nAddie Knox scored on a corner with 11 seconds remaining in regulation, boosting the Warriors to a 2-1 victory over top-seeded Stephen Decatur in the Class 2A East Region II championship in Berlin.\nEaston (11-3), which has won seven straight, is seeded fourth in the Class 2A state tournament and will host fifth-seeded Hereford (11-3) on Thursday at 3 p.m. in a quarterfinal match.\n\"They never give up,\" Easton head coach Kim Neff said of her team during a phone interview Wednesday. \"They never come off the field thinking like, 'We're done.'\"\nDecatur (11-4) took a 1-0 lead in the second quarter on Jill Burton's goal, and carried that lead into halftime. But the Warriors didn't panic.\n\"I feel like this is our MO really,\" Neff said. \"We're used to coming from behind. We don't stress too much about it. We knew we had plenty of time to get back in that game. And I told them, 'Just go put a goal in right now and score and tie it up.' And sure enough they went and tied it up.\"\nLess than 2 minutes into the second half, Easton's Myka Motovidlak smacked a drive toward the goal that was knocked into the cage by Georgia Spies for a 1-1 tie.\n\"We have faced a lot of challenges this season,\" Neff said. \"Not a lot of teams have. Some teams it comes a little easier to win. I feel running into the playoffs that's an advantage for us. We know we can come from behind. We know we can go to double overtime and win. We've experienced that. I feel like that's an advantage for us.\"\nPlay evened out through the rest of the third quarter. The Seahawks then got a string of corners in the fourth quarter, but could not get anything else past Easton's defense of Bis Johnson, Kadence McGuckin, Lea Boutte and freshman goalie Taylor Bowen (12 saves).\n\"Our goalie saved the day,\" Neff said of Bowen, whose only experience in goal prior to this season was in rec league play. \"Taylor just did a phenomenal job. She's so coachable and she sees the field. And she's so athletic. She just impressed all of us.\"\nEaston survived Decatur's flurry of corners and worked the ball back into the Seahawks end with about 2 minutes remaining. It was then that Neff turned to assistant Katie Spies and said they needed to start thinking about who they were going to put on the field for the first overtime period.\nBut with a little under a minute to play, Easton's Ryan Quicke drew a foul, setting up a corner.\n\"We got in a little huddle right before we got the corner and Stella (Kabler) was like, 'This is it guys,'\" Knox said. \"Then I looked up at the scoreboard and it said 50 seconds left. And when (Neff) called that Liv (Olivia Orrell) was taking the direct shot, I was like, 'This is it.' Because Liv always gets it in there.\"\nKnox inserted the ball off the end line, then moved to the left post. Orrell sent a drive that was stopped by Decatur's goalie. But the ball bounced upward toward Knox, who batted the ball into the cage for a 2-1 Warriors lead.\n\"It was great,\" Knox said. \"Everybody just jumped up. I couldn't even breath.\"\nBut while Easton's players were celebrating, Neff was pleading.\n\"Everybody was losing their mind except me who was saying, 'We still have 11 seconds left,'\" Neff said. \"'Do not let them go down and get in the circle.'\"\nDecatur rushed downfield and got close to the circle before Johnson swept the ball out of bounds, leaving the Seahawks not enough time to retrieve the ball and mount one last threat.\n\"They believe in themselves and they believe in their teammates,\" Neff said. \"It's really an awesome group of girls.\" \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 10,
    "day": 30,
    "llm_classification": {
      "topic": "Sports",
      "explanation": "The article reports on a high school field hockey game, detailing scores, players, and coach comments, which clearly falls under the Sports category."
    },
