  {
    "title": "K. Island topples Q. Anne's for title",
    "date": "2024-11-08",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "K. Island topples Q. Anne's for title\n\n November 8, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 149\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n CENTREVILLE — Gianna King had 16 kills, 11 digs and five aces Wednesday, and sophomore Madison Parks had the game-winning block in the fifth game, as Kent Island High's volleyball team defeated top-seeded and unbeaten Queen Anne's County, 25-18, 19-25, 25-17, 23-25, 15-10 to win the Class 2A East Region II championship.Kent Island (14-2) will be seeded second in the Class 2A state tournament and host No. 7 Williamsport in a quarterfinal on Saturday at 11 a.m.\nMacayla Kirk finished with 11 kills, 10 digs and one ace for the Buccaneers, who lost both regular-season matches to the defending region-champion Lions. Alaina Dlabich totaled 16 assists, nine digs and two aces, and Payton Goldfein netted eight kills and a block.\nKent Island also got contributions from Abbigail Fisher (six digs, three aces, assist), Parks (four blocks, kill), Lauren Wigglesworth (three kills, two blocks) and Madison Saville (five digs, four aces). \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
