  {
    "title": "Queen Anne's shuts down Warriors",
    "date": "2024-12-17",
    "author": "Bill Haufe",
    "content": "Queen Anne's shuts down Warriors\n\n December 17, 2024 | Star Democrat, The (Easton, MD)\n\n Author/Byline: Bill Haufe | Section: Sports \n \n 636\n Words \n\n Read News Document\n\n EASTON — While his offense may be the most dynamic he's had in years as Queen Anne's County High's girls head basketball coach, defense has been Mike Kern's greater focus early this season.The Lions gave Easton a heavy dose of both Tuesday night.\nDamiya Henry scored 16 points, Karianna Hickson had 14, and Queen Anne's, after yielding 10 first-quarter points, only allowed 10 over the final three quarters on the way to a 52-20 victory over the Warriors.\nThe Lions improved to 5-0 overall, 3-0 North Bayside, setting up Thursday's early division clash with Cambridge-South Dorchester (4-0, 2-0) in Centreville.\n\"I'm looking for good defense,\" said Kern, whose team trailed 10-9 after the first quarter. \"We gave up 10 points in the first quarter and then I think we gave up 10 the rest of the game. I think it's one of those things we've got to play good defense. We can't give up easy baskets. We've got to move more, contest every shot.\"\nKi'Mauri Lewis scored on a drive to give Easton (1-3, 1-1) an early 2-0 lead. Queen Anne's moved to a 5-2 lead, but Serenity Velez buried a 3-pointer and Lewis scored from the baseline for a 7-5 Warriors lead with 3:51 left in the first quarter.\nA pair of Hickson free throws and a Laila Coles layup off a backdoor cut nudged the Lions back in front at 9-7 with 2 minutes left in the first. But freshman Maia Bailey connected on a 3 that gave Easton a 10-9 lead heading into the second quarter.\n\"I thought Easton did a great job driving,\" Kern said. \"We've got to cut the drive off. We've got to slide our feet and get in position.\n\"They're very athletic,\" Kern added of Easton. \"They pressured us, played us in a man, and it took us a little while to figure it out. And then on the defensive end they were probably a little quicker than we anticipated. We made a couple of adjustments, and I think once we settled down we started playing better.\"\nThe Lions did just that while taking control of the game in the second quarter. Hickson scored 12 straight points, which included a pair of 3-pointers, Cheyanne Hollis scored on a putback, and Coles hit a free throw for a 15-0 run that gave Queen Anne's a 24-10 lead.\n\"Hickson came out big in the first half,\" Kern said.\nVelez hit a basket with 7.3 seconds left in the half for Easton's only points of the quarter.\n\"Excellent first quarter,\" Easton head coach Lesley Staehli said of her team. \"Then we stopped moving on offense and we got a little lazy on defense. I think that hurt us. We went into halftime with high spirits. Just being within arm's length of them is a positive for us with how good they are. They move the ball well. They cut well.\"\nQueen Anne's maintained its 12-point cushion at 26-14 with 4:24 left in the third quarter.\nThen Henry, who played at Easton two years ago and was at Cambridge-SD last season before transferring to Queen Anne's, scored eight consecutive points that extended the Lions lead to 36-14 with 1:10 remaining in the third quarter.\n\"Henry showed off tonight for sure,\" Staehli said with a smile of her former player. \"Totally miss that kid. Definitely would have done us some good to have her this year. And she went out in two quarters and led the team.\"\nEaston ended a 6-minute scoring drought when Velez canned a 3-pointer with 40 seconds left in the third quarter, making it 36-17 Lions.\nDefending North Bayside-champions Queen Anne's then reeled off the first 14 points of the fourth quarter to widen its lead to 50-17 with just under 3 minutes left.\nVelez and Bailey each had eight points to lead Easton.\nQueen Anne's Bea Holthaus had nine points, 16 rebounds and blocked three shots. \n\n © Copyright © 2024 Star Democrat, Chesapeake Publishing Group (Adams Publishing/APGMedia). All rights reserved.",
    "content_source": "full_document",
    "year": 2024,
    "month": 12,
    "day": 17,
